Chapter: DeskTaskbarHitTest
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Works chapter GopFont
  cites UI chapter Widget
  cites UI chapter Layout
  cites UI chapter Event
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The taskbar's system-menu entry reaches the launcher by the same road the
 sidebar's `Programs` button does: `desk-dispatch` folds both ids into one
 `prg`, so there is one dispatch and not two. This asserts the half a capture
 cannot -- that a pointer landing on the entry resolves to `menu` and not to
 the band behind it -- and pins the band geometry the clock paints into.

 The rows below the band are the root panel's own padding, so the band does
 not reach the screen edge. It is printed rather than asserted because it is
 the theme's number, not this file's.

 THE BAND IS NO LONGER A CONSTANT AND THIS ARM NO LONGER ASSERTS ONE. It used
 to read `band height is dk-task-h`, which is a statement about a number
 rather than about what the band promises: when the entry's height was lifted
 the band laid out taller and that row went red for a change that fixed
 something. What it promises is that the entry inside it can hold a line of
 the face, and that is what is asserted now -- against the CONTRACT rather
 than against another instance of the same arithmetic (L-BOTHARMS).

 THE FACE IS SYNTHETIC, and it has to be. `gfont-load` needs a volume and the
 battery attaches none, so a face-path assertion here would record the
 no-volume line and prove nothing (L-NAMED). A `GopFont` is a plain record:
 `gf-ok` true and a `gf-gh` of 18 is the CMUNSS cell at the ppem this desk
 uses below 1600, measured, and it is all `dk-task-btn-h` reads. The tree is
 measured DIRECTLY rather than through `desk-chrome-face`, because that path
 runs `comp-fit-text`, which would measure text through a face whose glyph
 base is zero.

 The faceless rows are the control and they must NOT move: the bitmap cell
 fits the band it has, so the entry asks for nothing there and the band stays
 at its floor. A change that grew both would be a change nobody needed.

Section: Body

  tb-yn : Boolean -> Text
  tb-yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "no"

  tb-face : GopFont
  tb-face = GopFont { gf-ok = True, gf-base = 0, gf-gw = 0, gf-gh = 18, gf-asc = 0, gf-cap = 0 }

  tb-hit-id : WidgetNode, Integer, Integer -> Text
  tb-hit-id (laid) (x) (y) =
    when ev-hit-widget laid x y
      is Just (w) -> w.wn-id
      is None -> "-"

  tb-rect : WidgetNode, Text -> LayoutRect
  tb-rect (laid) (id) =
    when widget-find laid id
      is Just (w) -> w.wn-bounds
      is None -> layout-rect 0 0 0 0

  tb-chrome : Integer, Integer -> WidgetNode
  tb-chrome (w) (ds) = desk-chrome-with (widget-panel "content" DirColumn 0 []) w ds

  tb-min-h : WidgetNode, Text -> Integer
  tb-min-h (root) (id) =
    when widget-find root id
      is Just (n) -> n.wn-min-h
      is None -> 0 - 1

 The cache is written by `desk-run` and by nothing a gated arm reaches, so
 without this the reading half of `dk-task-px` would be a path nothing calls
 (L-UNCALLED). Both answers are asserted: the fallback an unwritten cell
 gives, and the cached value once one is there.

  tb-cached : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tb-cached (ds) (v) = let p = poke-32 ds dk-task-band-cell v in ds

  tb-band : Integer, Integer, GopFont, Text -> Text
  tb-band (w) (ds) (tf) (tag) =
    let ws = ui-wscale w
    in let m = widget-measure (desk-taskbar ds tf ws) (dk-theme-ds ds)
    in let band = m.wn-min-h
    in let entry = tb-min-h m "menu"
    in let cell = dk-task-btn-h tf ws
    in tag & " band " & integer-to-text band
       & " entry " & integer-to-text entry
       & " asks " & integer-to-text cell
       & "  band at least its floor " & tb-yn (band >= dk-task-h)
       & "  entry holds a line " & tb-yn (entry >= cell)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let ds = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let ap = poke-32 ds dk-adorn-cell dk-adorn-default
    in let gp = poke-32 ds desk-gpu-cell 1
    in let sd = widget-layout (tb-chrome 1024 ds) (dk-theme-ds ds) (layout-rect 0 0 1024 768)
    in let hd = widget-layout (tb-chrome 1600 ds) (dk-theme-ds ds) (layout-rect 0 0 800 450)
    in let band = tb-rect sd "taskbar"
    in let mb = tb-rect sd "menu"
    in let cb = tb-rect sd "task-clock"
    in let hb = tb-rect hd "taskbar"
    in act
      print-line-uni ("band is at least its floor: " & tb-yn (band.lr-h >= dk-task-h))
      print-line-uni ("logical rows below band  : " & integer-to-text (768 - (band.lr-y + band.lr-h)))
      print-line-uni ("menu inside the band     : " & tb-yn (mb.lr-y >= band.lr-y & mb.lr-y + mb.lr-h <= band.lr-y + band.lr-h))
      print-line-uni ("menu centre resolves to  : " & tb-hit-id sd (mb.lr-x + mb.lr-w / 2) (mb.lr-y + mb.lr-h / 2))
      print-line-uni ("clock right of the menu  : " & tb-yn (cb.lr-x > mb.lr-x + mb.lr-w))
      print-line-uni ("clock ends inside band   : " & tb-yn (cb.lr-x + cb.lr-w <= band.lr-x + band.lr-w))
      print-line-uni ("band height at 1600      : " & integer-to-text (hb.lr-h))
      print-line-uni (tb-band 1024 ds gfont-none "1024 bitmap")
      print-line-uni (tb-band 1024 ds tb-face   "1024 face  ")
      print-line-uni (tb-band 1600 ds gfont-none "1600 bitmap")
      print-line-uni (tb-band 1600 ds tb-face   "1600 face  ")
      print-line-uni ("dk-task-px unwritten     : " & integer-to-text (dk-task-px ds 1024))
      print-line-uni ("dk-task-px from the cache: " & integer-to-text (dk-task-px (tb-cached ds 34) 1024))
    end

